      "standardized_narrative": "At 1 January 2019 gross claims outstanding were GBP 830.4m. The syndicate did not disclose an explicit aggregate prior-year reserve movement amount in the financial statements; additionally the 2017 Year of Account was reinsured-to-close into 2018 (RITC GBP 219.3m), which distorts claims development analysis. Management reports mixed reserve developments across classes: material exposures from 2018 large losses (Hurricane Michael, Typhoon Jebi, Camp and Woolsey wildfires and a Lurssen shipyard loss) saw both deterioration (e.g. Jebi and Lurssen) and improvement (Camp and Woolsey), and 2019 typhoons (Hagibis, Faxai) produced gross exposures with net impacts described as immaterial. Overall the syndicate describes mixed prior-year development and does not provide a single quantified prior-year reserve release or strengthening.",
      "raw_causal_phrases": [
        "The high incidence of catastrophe and large losses seen in 2018 and 2019 has had a positive impact on the rating environment across a number of classes including Energy, Financial Institutions and Management Liability.",
        "The Syndicate has gross material exposure to Typhoon Hagibis and Typhoon Faxai in the 2019 Year of Account. The net exposure to these losses are immaterial.",
        "Last year, the Syndicate had material exposure to the Hurricane Michael, Typhoon Jebi, the Camp and Woolsey Wildfires and the Lurssen Shipyard loss in the 2018 Year of Account. During the year, the exposure to Typhoon Jebi and Lurseen Shipyard have deteriorated; however, there has been an improvement for the Camp and Woolsey Wildfires."
